 {r}←DeleteSupersededFiles folder;stems;years;superseded
⍝ Deletes the usage data files in `folder` that are not needed any more, the CSV and the ZIP alike.
⍝ A file for a year up to a month, like "usage-data-2025-08", holds all data of that year so far,
⍝ so it is superseded by any later file of the same year:
⍝ * by a later one up to a month, like "usage-data-2025-10"
⍝ * by the file for the whole year, "usage-data-2025"
⍝ Files for whole years always stay, and so does anything else in the folder, like the log file
⍝ and its backups.
 r←⍬
⍝ Newest first, the file for a whole year ahead of those up to a month: see `ListUsageDataFiles`
 stems←∪{⍵↓⍨-≢'.csv'}¨'*'##.ListUsageDataFiles folder
 years←{4↑⍵↓⍨≢'usage-data-'}¨stems
 superseded←(⍳≢years)≠years⍳years                  ⍝ Anything but the newest file of its year
 :If ∨/superseded
     {}##.F.DeleteFile¨,(folder∘,¨superseded/stems)∘.,'.csv' '.zip'
 :EndIf
⍝Done
